<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?><gpx xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance" xmlns:groundspeak="http://www.groundspeak.com/cache/1/0/1" xmlns:xsd="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema" version="1.0" creator="Groundspeak, Inc.All Rights Reserved.http://www.groundspeak.com" xsi:schemaLocation="http://www.topografix.com/GPX/1/0 http://www.topografix.com/GPX/1/0/gpx.xsd http://www.groundspeak.com/cache/1/0/1 http://www.groundspeak.com/cache/1/0/1/cache.xsd" xmlns="http://www.topografix.com/GPX/1/0"><name>Cache Listing Generated from Geocaching.com</name><desc>This is an individual cache generated from Geocaching.com</desc><email>contact@geocaching.com</email><url>http://www.geocaching.com</url><urlname>Geocaching - High Tech Treasure Hunting</urlname><time>2026-03-02T05:14:12.7458703Z</time><keywords>cache, geocache</keywords><wpt lat="39.428867" lon="-84.4299"><time>2023-09-16T00:00:00</time><name>GCAE96C</name><desc>Everyday Is Halloween by Sarahshaw20</desc><url>https://www.geocaching.com/geocache/GCAE96C</url><urlname>Everyday Is Halloween</urlname><sym>Geocache</sym><type>Geocache|Traditional Cache</type><groundspeak:cache id="9250011" available="true" archived="false"><groundspeak:name>Everyday Is Halloween</groundspeak:name><groundspeak:placed_by>Sarahshaw20</groundspeak:placed_by><groundspeak:owner id="44129857">Sarahshaw20</groundspeak:owner><groundspeak:type>Traditional Cache</groundspeak:type><groundspeak:container>Regular</groundspeak:container><groundspeak:attributes><groundspeak:attribute id="1" inc="1">Dogs</groundspeak:attribute><groundspeak:attribute id="25" inc="1">Parking nearby</groundspeak:attribute><groundspeak:attribute id="28" inc="1">Public restrooms nearby</groundspeak:attribute><groundspeak:attribute id="17" inc="1">Poisonous plants</groundspeak:attribute><groundspeak:attribute id="39" inc="1">Thorns</groundspeak:attribute></groundspeak:attributes><groundspeak:difficulty>1.5</groundspeak:difficulty><groundspeak:terrain>2.5</groundspeak:terrain><groundspeak:country>United States</groundspeak:country><groundspeak:state>Ohio</groundspeak:state><groundspeak:short_description /><groundspeak:long_description>&lt;p&gt;With October coming I wanted to get a Halloween cache out. I use to have a cache in this park, but it was washed away in flooding. This one will not be washed away. Halloween is my favorite Holliday and all the spooky fun that goes on all month. I have filled this cache with lots of creepy items for trade. Please leave something if you take something. No worries if what you leave isn&amp;#39;t Halloween related but great if it is. I love Dudley Woods Metropark. Enjoy your hike and stay spooky! Oh and please leave the syringe pen for the log. &lt;br /&gt;
🎉Congrats to Intrepid Dyad on Super fast FTF!!&lt;/p&gt;
</groundspeak:long_description><groundspeak:encoded_hints>Between Gregory Creek and main trail.</groundspeak:encoded_hints><groundspeak:logs><groundspeak:log id="1341136258"><groundspeak:date>2026-01-05T15:51:45</groundspeak:date><groundspeak:type>Found it</groundspeak:type><groundspeak:finder id="52414534">rustedrat</groundspeak:finder><groundspeak:text encoded="false">Was taking a regular old stroll when I came across this. Will have to come back by with a trinket </groundspeak:text></groundspeak:log><groundspeak:log id="1321521368"><groundspeak:date>2025-08-31T11:34:04</groundspeak:date><groundspeak:type>Write note</groundspeak:type><groundspeak:finder id="44129857">Sarahshaw20</groundspeak:finder><groundspeak:text encoded="false">If the trail is too over grown you can always walk up the river bed. </groundspeak:text></groundspeak:log><groundspeak:log id="1299641062"><groundspeak:date>2025-05-19T12:00:00</groundspeak:date><groundspeak:type>Found it</groundspeak:type><groundspeak:finder id="1148650">SM325</groundspeak:finder><groundspeak:text encoded="false">The Mighty Three were out for another weekly Zany Geocaching Adventure (ZGA) invading the cities of Springdale, Mount Heathy, Dent, Bridgetown and Delhi.

As I am limited mobility, I used my power chair to reach GZ.  The trail began near the restrooms and was wide and flat.  Next, the trail branches to the right with a bridge (with no steps) went across a stream.  The path after bridge was narrower, but still good.  Tazzy really enjoyed this stretch and picked up lots of new smells.

Once we reached the "Oak Trail .24 mile" sign we took the short trail to the right which stopped at the river.  Finally, we turned left on a narrow (maybe one foot wide?) path which paralleled the river.  We used the CO's coordinates of **N 39° 25.724' W 84º 25.784'** which took us straight to the unique container.

Note to future geocachers: You'll want to bring bug spray as we donated about a  pint of blood to skeeters.  Thanks so much for putting this one out as well as feeding my insatiable addiction!  The log sheet was signed BTS for br549*, Tazzy and SM325.</groundspeak:text></groundspeak:log><groundspeak:log id="1299460464"><groundspeak:date>2025-05-19T10:35:09</groundspeak:date><groundspeak:type>Found it</groundspeak:type><groundspeak:finder id="15369726">br549*</groundspeak:finder><groundspeak:text encoded="false"> I am out with SM325 and Tazzy on todays adventure in geocaching. It is supposed to be nice today with a high in the 70’s.  We are knocking out a number of different types today. Our goal is to get 30 today. Thanks. </groundspeak:text></groundspeak:log><groundspeak:log id="1291800804"><groundspeak:date>2025-04-16T17:03:38</groundspeak:date><groundspeak:type>Found it</groundspeak:type><groundspeak:finder id="461191">tmbrrun</groundspeak:finder><groundspeak:text encoded="false">Nice day for a hike along a trail. Thanks for the cache. </groundspeak:text></groundspeak:log></groundspeak:logs></groundspeak:cache></wpt><wpt lat="39.431602277510535" lon="-84.43001747131348"><time>2023-09-16T13:11:18</time><name>P0AE96C</name><cmt /><desc>Parking lot</desc><url>https://www.geocaching.com/seek/wpt.aspx?WID=f53f3428-7a75-4cd2-beb1-ecd1b31eb09b</url><urlname>Parking lot</urlname><sym>Parking Area</sym><type>Waypoint|Parking Area</type></wpt></gpx>